{"title":"Metric (analysis)","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>metric</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/b/00badc562b4d2b96505832d17476a4082cfd7544.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d: S \\times S \\to \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"112\" height=\"13\" /> which obeys the following three properties:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Symmetry: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67c87ea51d3289aaec35c3743d64e813e449f7e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(x, y) = d(y, x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> for all points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/9/329f47e47ef81bd7de1b7041b1f3ab4bfaf796f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />.</li>\n<li>Positivity: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aabce2eeefcac68f27af9526e78b2fbddf372e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(x, y) \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/9/329f47e47ef81bd7de1b7041b1f3ab4bfaf796f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/5/7c51491db86008b1eb7252e51d25f08fd49a798e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(x, y) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e33fa7c7b2ce1a18e6e0a6d3ef6c08bd1958722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />.</li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Triangle inequality\">triangle inequality</a>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/3/1a3323549bde595dc1922ea4773b3b67dab5aab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(x, y) + d(y, z) \\geq d(x, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"198\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/2/3c25f77b4c978582e3cf1564cd15ddb8f70f6232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>Together, the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and the metric <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> form a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Metric_space\" title=\"Metric space\">metric space</a>.\n</p><p>Every metric space can be used to form a topology by considering taking the set of open balls as a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Topological_basis&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Topological basis (page does not exist)\">topological basis</a> (i.e. the sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/4972bcce6081cd7fd164e4579f3fdfc250c3588e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{x,\\epsilon}:=\\{y\\in S:d(x,y)&lt;\\epsilon\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Common_metrics\">Common metrics</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Metric_(analysis)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Common metrics\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d920e2010bf952bdef6df4036e6996593989deb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\mathbb{R}^n$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euclidean_metric\" title=\"Euclidean metric\">Euclidean metric</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d56fd6d5f11bd01130653c25d90e2e33768fe75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d((x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n), (y_1, y_2, \\ldots y_n)) = \\sqrt{(x_1-y_1)^2 + \\ldots + (x_n - y_n)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"521\" height=\"32\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematical_convention\" title=\"Mathematical convention\"> conventional</a> distance function.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>For any set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discrete_metric\" title=\"Discrete metric\">discrete metric</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/4/254179f4551f75c959cbe6efef724cda314f7a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(x, y) = 0 \\Longleftrightarrow x = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23b8609278c932224bff85394319a604e0a7d90a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(x, y) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> otherwise.</li></ul>\n<p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Metric_(analysis)&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018071247\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 99/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3556/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.134      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.134      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3944:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018071247 and revision id 110287. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}